      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-04-16_WidnesExaminer_art0036" n="art0036">
        <head>RETURN OF THE DISCOVERY.</head>
        <p>THE RETURN OF THE DISCOVERY.</p>
        <p>The safe arrival of the Discovery Antarctic Expedition in New Zealand and the latest news of the doings and discoveries of Captain Scott and his brave crew are exciting the keenest interest on every side. Only one little incident has occurred to mar the harmony of the home-corn- ing; and that is to a certain extent shrouded in mystery. Two inde pen- dent correspon- dents cabled from Christ- church, New Zealand, to he effect hat Captain Scott considered the despatch o f the Terra Nova wasteful and unneces- sary, and he has telegraphed home an indig- nant denial of the statement.</p>
        <p>Apart from this little con- tretemps everything is well and satisfactory. The Discovery,it will be remembered, left Cowes ua August, 1901, after a farewell visit from the King and Queen; and on Christmas Eve of that year, she left Port Chalmers, ' gew Zealand. From that date up till a few days ago the majority of her crew have been ice-bound beyond the ken of their fellow creatures. Last year news of. them and their accomplishments was brought back by the Morning, which had on board, amongst others, Lieutenant Shackleton of the Discovery, who gave a very detailed and interesting account of the first year s affairs. Amongst other things Wilkes Land, which has been charted on the maps for many years, has been found to be non-existent; and it has been ascertained that the Great Ice Barrier is moving northward at the annual rate of a quarter of a mile. A new form of insect life, the snow flea, has been dis- covered, and fresh information about various birds, including the emperor penguin: and a few lichens and mosses are added to our knowledge of the vegetable world, as well as certain fossilised forms of plant life.</p>
        <p>...,;.:7-... _____,_:,-' •-• •••,* • :/"' , ..1........ t ' ...' t r . . ;•• ' -'4 . '''' , . . '0)• , , , ~,,Vtili ' " "1' ._4‘' '.'‘ ' ' • l/1/_:' "C-i/. ,:. 7- ' 1 •.s.rx" ~.; '' /./ ‘:. ,:::*, ~.,\},.\, t? ;ii• ' a I/ / t'4, V \ • • // N CAPTAIN SCOTT.</p>
