        <head>NORTHERN UNION.</head>
        <p>THE NORTHERN UNION.</p>
        <p>THE FIRST DIVISION.</p>
        <p>Wit WARRINGTON v. LEEDS. Wa With the exception that Kenyon deputised Fish, en, nitigton placed a full team in the field against Leeds tho Saturday. The visitors were strongly represented as ugh Jenkins was an absentee. About 4,000 spectators gesernbled,and the conditions would have been ideal but aarciaomst_ro.ang wind blowing from goal to goal. Teams Le "i,el Is : It eus—H. Littlewood, back; W. Evans,T. Llewellyn, ,ticiWard and G. Andrew, three-quarter backs ; G. Grace IV, P. Mosley, half backs • J. G. Moffat, G. Hewlett, ansiNoolf,H. Moon, T. Tayfor,J. W. Birch, J. W. Stead, wk.% Wormald, forwards. pir,Larrington— Hallam, back; Kenyon, Isherwood, aocignson, and Harris, three-quarter backs; Davies Thokenhall, half backs; Fairhurst, Swift, Cook, "4") Edmondson, Morrison, Lunt, and Jolley, for- Ab --tee, Mr. J. Oaklandaakefteld.Touch judges, Mr. le4l, Runcorn, and J. H. Houghton, St. Helens. bute.e,_(lB had the advantage of the wind in the first half, - eY inade poor use of it. First Littlewood and eaej; alosley tried at goal from penalty kicks, but in 114-4- ease the effort was unsuccessful. Davies made s try; el,,Lort for Warrington, a pass forward spiling the tom."-no home side played up gtrengly afterwards, eiyi riGhlnation between Isherwood, Dickenson, and Harris, lit(3at 11ave ended in a score had the last-named not _, on in taking the final transfer. After 35 44%4'1_8 play, Dickenson picked up in the loose in the e flair and getting well away passed at the right 1,,,a7tt0 Hockenhall, who completed a clever moye. faiimoY grounding the ball over the Leeds line. Davies 1114r11;arat.tbgreoaailawLay by Mosley pressed severely afterwards, and Mosley was just checked in time °ver ni„lia,ni, • From a cross kick by Grace, Evans ran cki Lae right corner, but the referee overruled the had T, for a try, presumably on the ground ttiatsEvans tery -Ilocked on in taking the ball. Just before the in- at hal Littlewood kicked a penalty goal, and the score of pr-time 